.TH WELLMEM 1 "August 2026" "wellmem 1.3" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
wellmem \- memory usage overview
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellmem
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellmem
prints a colour-coded summary of memory usage read directly from
.IR /proc/meminfo :
total, used (total minus available), buffers, cache (Cached plus
SReclaimable), shared, free, and swap usage, with a usage bar.
.PP
When stdout is a terminal the report is drawn as boxes; when piped a plain
layout is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language (default \fBauto\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output without box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when piped.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON on stdout; errors still go to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unexpected runtime error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in auto mode.
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1),
.BR wellhw (1)
